From 183ea86e6e0f9166bdfa549552d4e537d52d68bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] SEO: live title and description templates; app and HTML
 titles match

Listing titles: the reviewed programme name, plus the org when the name
doesn't already say who runs it, the programme year and the next date
('Research Science Institute (MIT / CEE): Deadline Dec 11 | HSO'; the
Treasury internship now says 'U.S. Treasury'). Parts drop in order to stay
within about 65 characters; past deadlines are never shown.

Descriptions are facts first and under 155 characters: Free / Paid stipend /
Tuition or fee, grades, place, apply-by or opening date, then the first line
of the blurb. They come from live data, so they no longer carry frozen dates
from the reviewed copy (Duke Math Meet's still said Oct 25).

Guide pages and the homepage now read their title, description and JSON-LD
from STATIC_PAGE_META, the same source the prerender uses, so the title no
longer changes after the page loads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
